    skos:prefLabel "On Site Volatile Headspace Testing by Photo Ionisation Detector"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote
        "Group rules: IPID_RES shall generally be numeric data. A text form shall only be used by addition of a prefixing operator to denote greater than or less than conditions i.e. >200 when readings are above the reporting limit of the testing equipment."@en ,
        """IPID is used to record the results of on-site volatile testing by means of headspace analysis using photo ionisation detectors.
IPID_CRED added to permit details of any test accreditation if appropriate to be included in data.
Clause 7.9.8 of the updated SISG Specification advises ambient weather and temperature to be recorded at time of test. IPID_ENV and IPID_TEMP added to include this information."""@en ;
