    skos:notation "CPTT"^^xsd:token ;
    skos:prefLabel "Cone Penetration Test (CPT/CPTu) - Data"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote """CPTT is used to include the readings from the cone converted from the measurement data using any required calibration factors and other mathematical formulae employed by the measurement contractor in accordance with the specification.
Readings included in group will depend on the test carried out. For example, the ground parameters measured and included in this group will depend on test type / cone.
The fluorescence intensity, photo-multiplier tube readings, PID, FID and conductivity data require graphic interpretation. These have been removed.
CPTT_BDEN and CPTT_ISPP allow for complex assumptions on density and piezometric profiles. Explanation of these assumptions is required within CPTG_REM.
The requirements for transfer of data in CPTT should be fully specified at the outset of testing in the investigation specification.
Vertical offset corrections shall have been applied, e.g. the cone sleeve offset, so that a row of readings is for the soil at CPTT_DPTH.
For T-bar and Ball Penetrometer use CPTT_QC, CPTT_QNET and CPTT_U1, CPTT_U2 or CPTT_U3 as applicable"""@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf <https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/dictionary> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://gitlab.com/AGS-DFWG-Web/ASG4/-/blob/710b1f08097264e6508be1397282aece79278fc4/AGS4/AGS4_2/4_2_0/groupsandheadings4-2-0.json> ;
    schema:status status:stable ;
    agso:groupClass ags:CPTT ;
    agso:parentGroup <https://w3id.org/ags4/voc/dictionary/CPTG> ;
.

